  "content": {
    "id": "p2-q7-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "7",
    "prompt": "Suppose the point $P(x,y)$ is located at an equal distance from points $A(2,2)$ and $B(-1,3)$. Find a formula for $y$ in terms of $x$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$y=3x+1$.\n\nEquate the squared distances $PA^2$ and $PB^2$.",
      "worked": "Since $PA=PB$:\n$$\\begin{align*}PA^2&=PB^2\\\\(x-2)^2+(y-2)^2&=(x+1)^2+(y-3)^2\\\\x^2-4x+4+y^2-4y+4&=x^2+2x+1+y^2-6y+9\\\\-4x-4y+8&=2x-6y+10\\\\2y&=6x+2\\\\y&=3x+1\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 60
  },
